Orca is an IDE for running coding agents such as Claude Code, Codex and
OpenCode in parallel, each in its own git worktree and terminals, with
review, editing and task tools around them.

This port installs Orca's server, orcad, which upstream runs for
`orca serve`: it keeps projects, worktrees, terminals and agent sessions
on this machine, and paired clients provide the UI. Clients are the Orca
desktop app on Linux, macOS or Windows, the browser client the server
itself serves, and the Orca mobile app.

The server's JavaScript is taken from upstream's Linux release and runs
on www/node24; its native addons, node-pty and @parcel/watcher, are built
from source.
